   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hey All,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m working on running SNAPPER, and it really hates SNPs that are missing in all individuals of a &quot;species&quot;. Any ideas on how to filter out SNPs that are missing in all individuals of any population? Or even X% of individuals in any population?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>Renee<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "9UgwysXgCAAJ",
   "from": "renee....@gmail.com",
   "author": "be5831679f44e5dc",
   "date": "2022-04-07T08:03:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: Filter SNPs that are absent in any population",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "It seems like it could be a &quot;by pop&quot; extension to gl.filter.allna - filter any SNP that is na in any single pop? I&#39;ll see if I can rewrite unless anyone else has an idea."
    ],
    [
     3,
